{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"e282d01dfcf01a8a03a3efd02faf525bbc5f415a8cc9992d7c8298fbb65f7f7c","digest":{"component_or_area":"attestation substrate (op-cert foundation)","key_entities":["src/rebar/attest/opcert.py","src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","src/rebar/attest/__init__.py","registry.POLICY","rebar.opcert.v1","sshsig scheme",".rebar/trusted_environments.yaml","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py::material_fingerprint","verify_signature_result.schema.json","git merge-base --is-ancestor"],"problem_keywords":["operation certificate","asymmetric cryptography","Ed25519","environment key","signature verification","era rotation","replay protection","mutation detection","in-toto attestation"],"propositions":["Op-certs are produced and verified via the foundation substrate using Ed25519 environment keys, bound to a specific ticket, material fingerprint, and merged-log position","The certificate subject is an in-toto v1 Statement binding ticket ID, material fingerprint (16-hex sha256 truncation), and main commit SHA, preventing replay onto different tickets or mutated materials","Environment-key rotation uses explicit-SHA era validity: a key is valid at cert binding commit P iff added_at_commit is ancestor of P and revoked_at_commit is not, with two-phase verdict (certified, key_not_valid_at_era, or mismatch)","The op-cert verifier performs ancestry comparison on main branch commits and emits canonical verdict enum values matching verify_signature_result.schema.json","Material fingerprint is computed by the caller (plan-review gate) and treated as an opaque bound string by the substrate, protecting against ticket mutation"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785819147255318395,"uuid":"aa0398f7-c33a-44f4-8264-1fc5ad87b3ed"}